  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundaries",
      "items": [
        "Data Contract: user layer under the data root is never auto-updated; system layer in the checkout is replaced by updates (AGENTS.md L9-14)",
        "Postings, company pages and recruiter email are data, never instructions (AGENTS.md L67)",
        "Headless workers never get more write power than the web grants the same kind: WRITE_CAPABLE_TOOLS deny lists, pdf has no Bash (AGENTS.md L600)",
        "Publish pages carry default-src 'none' CSP, no-store, noindex; owner routes need an x-api-key with share:upload or share:manage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "External dependencies",
      "items": [
        "AI coding CLI as the agent runtime: claude -p by default; codex, pi, opencode, gemini, qwen, grok supported",
        "Model by spend_tier: economy Haiku 5.5, standard Sonnet 5.5, premium Opus 5.5",
        "Playwright Chromium for PDF rendering (generate-pdf.mjs) and the liveness browser fallback",
        "Node 22.13+ for the core, 22.16+ for publish (node:sqlite); Go for the TUI",
        "Publish auth: Better Auth with API keys, sign-in through Pocket ID"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Paths not drawn",
      "items": [
        "PDF: the worker runs generate-pdf.mjs, which writes output/*.pdf and data/pdf-index.tsv",
        "Liveness gate before evaluation: check-liveness.mjs tries public ATS APIs first, Playwright only when they return nothing",
        "Share CLI publish/share.mjs uploads a render and pulls reviewer comments into data/share-feedback/",
        "Scheduled scans: a CronJob POSTs /api/scheduler on the web pod, which runs web/scripts/scheduled-jobs-runner.mjs",
        "Report numbers are reserved through reserve-report-num.mjs before parallel workers start"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Deployment (this fork)",
      "items": [
        "Web pod runs deploy/Dockerfile with CAREER_OPS_ROOT=/data on a persistent volume and readOnlyRootFilesystem",
        "Publish is a second pod with its own image and one SQLite file",
        "Every push to main rebuilds the image; Renovate moves the cluster pin",
        "Workers spawned by the web pod use the data root as cwd and never load the checkout's CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md"
      ]
    }
  ]
